  "details": "As is playing VRChat means having everything but player volumes down low in order to be social. In worlds where there is music or immersive audio, it's great to be able to hear both, but a blanket setting isn't great to mess with when a player wants to enjoy both.\n\nAutomatically turning other volume sliders down just when someone is talking would allow for worlds to stay immersive with its audio, but still allow for others to be heard clearly. Ideally this could be a setting that applies for anyone within earphone radius or specifically chosen (especially in the case of worlds where there is a public speaker).\n\nEven world developers could find use in detecting a players spoken volume. Worlds specifically meant to have a speaker, could create a system to dim ambient audio whenever appropriate while a player needs to be heard clearly. Alternatively games could be designed where players could have their volume gamified and have a ghost or something lured via loud noises. Some worlds as is have reverb applied to player voices and would be great if it could be taken a step further.",
